WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.300
Welcome to the Velvet Room.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.240
I see you have formed another new bond
after overcoming a fierce battle.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.470
It is the Lovers Arcana.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.180
I am certain this power will be of assistance.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.750
The Lovers, eh?

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.720
Taken in moderation,
romance can fertilize your heart,

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.880
but if taken to excess...

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.560
...it will prick you.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.080
glaciers of ideas importing

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.540
to my friends then exporting

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.950
to the next keeping it open

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:50.850
we want no closing

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.750
even without doughs
our thoughts can be dope and

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.220
this mind trade no one can stop

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.390
and act of thinking is terrible to stop

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.220
we just wanna change up not drop

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.120
and my crew can rock it like uprock

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.060
life is tedious if it ain't flowing

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.060
copy and paste? constant defaulting?

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.730
put my courage to it, begin showing off

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:06.900
that's the way we wanna live

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.730
keep going yeah

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.000
what was so much

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.130
of transparency

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:15.600
turned into bright expectation

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.640
my instinct tells me to keep going together

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.130
going together

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:29.150
it's breathtaking moments in life

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.350
addicted to it

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:33.060
minds craving

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.830
more and more

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.830
I'm believing

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.400
you and I can do anything

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.160
we can change the world

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.900
hey sky's the limit we can spread wings

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:55.610
to roadless travel together we go

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.160
Slim
Body

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.600
It's his fault.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.360
His fault! It's his!

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:19.900
CRITICAL HIT!!

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:20.500
DRAGON BOSS

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.200
MITSUO

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.440
Well? Did you see that?

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.340
I did it! I'm amazing.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.430
Wasn't this supposed to be a peaceful town?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.430
Dojima?

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.470
Serial murders, huh?

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:03.540
Damn it!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.880
What the hell?

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.390
I thought the victims were limited
to people shown on TV!

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.120
I've never seen King Moron on TV before.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.350
He didn't even appear on Midnight Channel.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.190
Damn, why'd this happen?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:23.960
I thought we figured some stuff out,
but maybe it was all a big coincidence.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.200
Midnight Channel might not even be
related to the murders.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.700
That can't be...

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.730
Then why's King Moron dead?

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:34.840
I don't know.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.770
M-my bad. I got short with you.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.790
This was beyond us.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:46.360
There's no way we could catch
someone eluding the cops.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.410
Huh? 'Scuse me?

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.750
Didn't you get involved
'cause it's over the cops' heads?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.470
The killer will stay at large
if we get weak-kneed now!

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.870
Are you cool with that?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.500
Huh?! None of us ordered this!

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.110
It's on the house.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.100
Normally we only offer this on rainy days.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:14.970
Th-that's!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.490
It takes Understanding to accept everything,
Knowledge to set a good pace,

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.220
Courage to attack the pile of meat,
and Diligence to keep eating.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:25.390
It takes all of that to finish off
this special nikudon!

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.590
Thanks, but why?

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.900
Eat before it gets cold.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.270
Well, let's chow down.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:35.740
20 Minutes Later

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:39.310
I eat and eat and still can't see the rice!
20 Minutes Later

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:39.600
20 Minutes Later

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.080
40 Minutes Later

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.650
Meat, meat, grease, grease and meat.
40 Minutes Later

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:44.980
40 Minutes Later

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.270
Seriously, what's with this monster?

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.820
But we've made a dent in it... I think.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:54.160
The serving's way too big!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.650
I don't think I'll reach the bottom.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.130
But we'll get there if we keep pressing on.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:06.140
Yeah, you're right. We'll get there
eventually if we keep at it.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.300
Mmhmm, I'm sure of it!

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.300
Yeah, damn straight!

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:16.550
We may not be able to see it now,
but regardless, we gotta keep going.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.910
I really can't see...

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:19.950
...the bottom of the bowl.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.310
That's all?!

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.680
You really are a weirdo.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.950
We gained a lot from that battle.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.660
It's 3,000 yen each.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.280
Wasn't it on the house?!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:37.700
If King Moron got thrown into the TV,
Kuma might know something.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.370
Right. Plus, I'm worried he's still deflated...

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.430
Huh? What're workers doing here?

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.110
I hope they haven't found out about the TV.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.180
Hi, there! Something the matter?

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.680
Oh, Yosuke! Great timing.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.950
A Mr. Kumada came by.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.450
Huh? Kumada?

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.830
This is bliss.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.130
Wow, he's here!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.660
This chair is pretty beariffic!

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.830
You look comfy.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.890
Wh-what are you doing here?

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.570
You finally showed up! I've been waiting.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:15.170
Kuma, is it wise to leave the TV?

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.510
You can?

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:19.840
Of course I can since there's an exit.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.210
It just never occurred to me before.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:27.770
But I got beary interested in your world
after hanging out with you.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.150
Yeah, that happens.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:33.720
I just knew Master would understand!

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.950
Oh, someone asked for my name,
so I said, "I'm Kuma, duh."

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.090
Thus the Kumada, huh?

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.160
Oh, Kumakichi! We need to ask you something.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.900
Huh?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.040
So you're absolutely positive
no one went into the TV?

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.810
That's what I keep saying!

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.870
I was all by my bearsome self
as I worked to recovery.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.340
Which means that King Moron
never went inside.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:02.550
So he was killed in our world...

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:10.090
Do you think the killer murdered him in the real
world since he wasn't succeeding with the TV?

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:15.330
Sounds likely. We've already saved
three people in a row.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.590
So he's getting impatient.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.470
Phew, I'm roasting!

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:22.370
Off it goes!

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:25.110
C-cut that out! Kids are watching!

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:29.270
Jeez! You'll scar the kids if they see
an empty mascot moving around.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.950
I'm not empty anymore!

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.210
Off it goes!

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:39.650
Phew, what a nice breeze!

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.560
Someone's inside him!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.060
Y-you're... Ehhh?!

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.790
N-no way...

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.630
I feel all revitalized!

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.430
I grew this in a jiffy
so Chie and Yukiko'd flirt with me.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.580
You grew insides? Just to flirt?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.940
How many times must you bring that up?

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:07.950
Say, got any clothes on hand?
I'm like a newborn babe.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.950
Don't you dare drop your drawers!

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.420
He needs clothes!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:12.750
He grew a human body inside himself?

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.790
Stop it!
He grew a human body inside himself?

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:15.820
Good for him.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.220
No friggin' way...

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.950
What the hell is that bear?!

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.650
Huh? Whatcha looking at, Dojima?

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.170
The people who recently went missing.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:31.230
I don't think they're unrelated
to the serial murders.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:36.470
More importantly, did you hear
about that boy detective?

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.210
The one helping with the investigation?

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.820
He's still a kid...

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:43.150
What were our superiors thinking?

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:46.990
It's no wonder since we haven't
made any progress.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:50.820
I blame this on you for bringing in that weirdo.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.530
Ouch!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:12.100
Uh, are you Kuma?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.080
Yes, that's right. What do you think?

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:17.450
Brilliant!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.390
Seriously, don't encourage him.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.490
No way. Who is he really?

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.860
I was shocked at first,
but he's definitely our Kuma.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:29.790
Honestly, he hasn't changed
to the point it's frustrating.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.970
He went nuts in the lady's department.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:35.200
I did?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.830
You can't follow your instincts
when you're in this form, got it?

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.440
This is my first time here...

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.680
Sorry. We aren't angry with you.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.620
Thank goodness! I was afraid you hate me now.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:53.510
Huh? Come to think of it, where's Kuma's head?

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.060
TOFU

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.360
Oh, they have some!

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.460
Pickled
Rice Bran
Radish Country
Pickled
Radish

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:18.610
What do you want? Got a problem?

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.510
You're rude, you damn brat.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.920
I'll show you what happens...

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:28.590
...if you cross me.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.560
Courage:
Fearless
Knowledge: Diligence:
Informed Staunch
Expression: Understanding:
Enthralling Generous

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.560
Courage:
Fearless
Knowledge: Diligence:
Informed Staunch
Expression: Understanding:
Enthralling Generous

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.470
Big Bro!

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:53.780
Can I help you?

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.910
Wh-who're you?

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:05.190
Are you okay?

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:08.600
Yeah. Thank you, Big Bro.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.620
But what are you doing here?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.260
Huh?

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.260
Ah!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.500
SUPER SPECIAL
40% OFF!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.980
Took ya long enough.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:22.640
I had to drop by my house.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.250
Oh, my pretty head!

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.480
I'm glad you came back to me.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:30.490
Thank you! Master, you're so nice.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:33.020
Isn't it great that you aren't empty anymore?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:35.390
Yeah, but...

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:40.560
I still don't know squat about myself.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:48.090
Let's look for the true inner you together.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.830
M-M-M-M-Master!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.140
Yeah! We'll catch the real me.

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.110
Why's he explodin' with energy?

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.280
He's been like this the whole time.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.410
It's like everything's new to him.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.740
Fine, take this.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.990
What's that for?

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.750
Get some popsicles and share 'em with Kuma.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.860
Wow, you're a rich man.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.690
That's Junes' prince for you.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:15.730
Oh, what's this, Hanamura?
You're acting like a senpai!

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:16.570
Huh?

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:20.300
I see. Hanamura, you really are an adult.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:25.210
Thank God you're an adult.
Adults don't sweat the small stuff, right?

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.380
I know you're up to something.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:33.280
See, we charged whatever we couldn't cover
with Kuma's clothes to your account.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:36.280
You what?! I'm paying?!

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:38.350
What the hell?! I never heard about this!

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:40.760
I can't help that we didn't have enough money.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.690
Junes' clothes are stupidly expensive.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:46.700
Okay, baby. Don't fight over me.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.430
Shut up! This is all your fault!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.200
Why'd you put it on my account without asking?!

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.300
C'mon, let's get some popsicles, Kuma.
Why'd you put it on my account without asking?!

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.540
C'mon, let's get some popsicles, Kuma.
Because I don't have any money!

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:53.870
Because I don't have any money!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.900
Give me a sec!
Because I don't have any money!

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:55.600
Give me a sec!
Then don't buy clothes!

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.610
These are for Rise.
You saying he was fine the way he was?

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:58.240
Master, please give them to her.
You saying he was fine the way he was?

00:12:58.240 --> 00:12:59.370
Master, please give them to her.
Of course not!

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:00.810
Sure, you got it.
Then what do you want?

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:01.410
At least cover half the tab!

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:02.080
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
At least cover half the tab!

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:02.440
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
No.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:02.940
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
Pay!

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:03.280
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
No.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:03.750
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
Pay!

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:04.110
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
No.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:04.910
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
Please pay.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:05.310
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
No.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:06.110
Say, this may take them a while,
so why don't we go?
I'll treat you!

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:06.410
Sounds good. Let's leave them be.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:07.250
Sounds good. Let's leave them be.
Then gimme a steak.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.680
Sounds good. Let's leave them be.
That defeats the point!

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:12.150
MARUKYU TOFU

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:19.720
My, I see you came after all.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.990
Huh? Aren't you...

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:24.230
Oh, dude!

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.100
What now?!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:27.930
It's him...

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.070
Here to appease Rise Kujikawa next?

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:36.770
Narukami!

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.110
Oh, so you're all here.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:43.650
I still haven't introduced myself.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:46.550
I'm Naoto Shirogane, a detective.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:52.130
I am currently helping the police
investigate the serial murders.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.060
A detective?

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:57.360
Right. Actually, may I ask for
your take on something?

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.100
Wh-what is it?

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:05.060
Wasn't our latest victim, Mr. Kinshiro Morooka,
a teacher at your school?

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.970
What of it?

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.980
The second victim, Saki Konishi,
attended the same school.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:15.080
The media is solely focusing on that,
but that isn't important.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.420
Something far more important is off.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:21.220
Like? What're you getting at?

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:25.720
Mr. Morooka was never aired on TV.

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:29.190
What does that mean?

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.220
Beats me.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:39.670
Very well. I simply want to close this case
as quickly as possible.

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:42.340
I've got my eye on you.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.540
Later.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:48.980
What was that about?

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.750
Sorry for bringing you out here.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:57.080
My grandma would get worried
if she overheard our discussion.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:59.220
Are you feeling any better?

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:01.300
I'm fine now.

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.400
But man, this bites.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:06.530
Risette, you sure you didn't see the guy's face?

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:09.870
Yeah. I was in the other world when I came to.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:12.800
It's just like with Kanji and me.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.100
